.TH SDL_SetRenderTarget 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_SetRenderTarget \- Set a texture as the current rendering target.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_render.h>
.PP
.BI "bool SDL_SetRenderTarget(SDL_Renderer *renderer, SDL_Texture *texture);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The default render target is the window for which the renderer was created\[char46] To stop rendering to a texture and render to the window again, call this function with a NULL
.BR texture \[char46]
.PP
Viewport, cliprect, scale, and logical presentation are unique to each render target\[char46] Get and set functions for these states apply to the current render target set by this function, and those states persist on each target when the current render target changes\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I renderer
the rendering context\[char46]
.TP
.I texture
the targeted texture, which must be created with the
.BR SDL_TEXTUREACCESS_TARGET
flag, or NULL to render to the window instead of a texture\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns true on success or false on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
This function should only be called on the main thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_GetRenderTarget (3)
